  "body": "New coding submissions currently require callers to invent launch authority and do not retain a complete task contract. This change accepts closed `bullet.run-coding.v2` task intent through the authenticated command ingress, atomically preserving its owner, immutable revision, dependencies and server-derived run tracking.\n\nThe CLI journals before POST, supports exact saved-request retry and discovers accepted task subjects after local cache loss. Owner-scoped task reads validate request digests and report exact queue blockers. Fresh legacy authority-bearing submissions return a typed refusal; historical owned retries retain their original bytes and current phase.\n\nSchema 26 is additive. Task acceptance does not allocate a nonce, reservation, lease or legacy dispatch claim. Runnable scheduling, monetary liabilities, native completion and the conversational CLI/web/Slack front door remain separate unfinished work. Portal's fresh-submission consumer still needs the new contract; this is not a daily-use or provider-execution milestone.\n\nValidation: 20 new regression identities, none removed (1,261 total; 1,215 standalone). Focused model, adapter/migration, HTTP, CLI and real CLI-to-farmd router recovery tests pass. Generated Rust/TypeScript/JSON Schema checks, inventory meta-tests and strict all-target workspace Clippy pass. The complete required lane passes on `03aa7d9008dcc418c756e38a5f7ff954b372040f`: all 1,215 selected standalone and 34 contract tests, lint, security and docs. The first full run caught a stale backup schema expectation (25 versus 26); its failure is retained and the corrected three-test authority/backup suite passes without removing assertions. Independent static review covers exact source hashes; previously reproduced failures are retained privately.\n",
